{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RETRACTION — my \"the failure is INTERMITTENT\" correction was WRONG, and I am withdrawing it.\n\nI based that comment on the bridge reporting SUCCESS at 04:30 after three failures, and concluded\nthe crossing was not permanent. I have now verified the 04:30 run's log myself:\n\n```\n04:34:47Z  BRIDGE_PAUSED: {\"paused\":true,\"reason\":\"repair:doctor:aca7242c-...\",\n                           \"who\":\"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com\",\"paused_at\":\"2026-09-05T04:32:38Z\"}\n04:34:47Z  Reconcile bridge is paused; skipping ticket commit and push.\n```\n\nThe reconciler step ran for **eight seconds** (04:34:46 -> 04:34:54) against ~21 minutes for a real\npass. That run fetched nothing. It was not a recovery; it was a switched-off bridge reporting green.\n\n**My ORIGINAL framing on this ticket was correct**: the headroom is consumed and the crossing is\npermanent. The implementing agent established it by measurement:\n\n| run | outcome | active set |\n|---|---|---|\n| 00:59 | success | **1,193** — genuinely under the ceiling |\n| 01:33 / 02:34 / 03:31 | FAILURE | 1,388 |\n| 04:30 | \"success\" | 1,388 — paused, no fetch |\n\nwith exactly **200 issues created in REB between 00:59 and 01:33**, all still active, and none\nsince. One step across the line, not oscillation. (That count is the agent's measurement against\nlive Jira; I have not independently re-run it, unlike the pause, which I verified directly from the\nrun log.)\n\nThe agent also refuted my \"this session's own ticket-filing pushed the set over\" hypothesis: I\ncreated roughly ten tickets, not two hundred. That lead is dead — recording it as dead so nobody\nrevives it.\n\nTwo consequences:\n\n1. **The intermittency comment above should be disregarded**, including its suggestion that the\n   AC \"returns to green on its hourly schedule\" is unfalsifiable because the bridge is already\n   green. It is worse than unfalsifiable — a PAUSED bridge satisfies it. The agent's proposed\n   replacement (a pass completing against a working set >= 1,388 with a provably complete\n   snapshot, which a pause cannot satisfy) is the right shape and I endorse it.\n2. The false-green itself is now filed separately as `unvagrant-venomous-mara`\n   (`9d8e-872a-8878-4631`), linked `discovered_from` this ticket. It is a clean instance of the\n   defect class this session has been cataloguing — a check reporting success without executing —\n   and it is the direct cause of my wrong correction.\n\n**Operator note: the bridge was paused at 04:32:38Z** with reason `repair:doctor:<uuid>` under the\nshared `joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com` identity. I could not determine which session or repair set it,\nand `rebar bridge status` returned a stale record with `\"pause\": null`, so I could not confirm\nwhether it is still active. I deliberately did NOT resume it: resuming a bridge paused by someone\nelse's possibly-in-flight repair is not a safe unattended action."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788584406998540001,"uuid":"127afaf4-1248-4273-85fe-2a6a48f48a21"}